[[1336,521,"In the narrative conclusion, the jury recorded a failure to prevent drugs from entering the prison.","drugs entering prison",""],[1337,521,"She did not read any part of his medical records before she saw him, and she did not know whether she was meant so to do. She was.","failure to review medical records",""],[1338,521,"She spoke to him through the hatch in the cell door, with his cellmate present.","insufficient patient interaction",""],[1339,521,"She did not have any meaningful discussion with him about his drug use, either the use that led to his collapse on 18 September 2024 or his use generally.","lack of drug use discussion",""],[1340,521,"She gave him various pieces of harm minimisation guidance in keeping with her training, including the advice to avoid using drugs whilst alone.","inadequate harm minimisation advice",""],[1341,521,"She did not know whether her interaction with Mr Campbell was in accordance with her training. I was told that it was not. She had not received further training or changed her practice since his death.","lack of training compliance",""],[7503,2884,"Healthcare staff seemed unclear as to how to fill in an Intelligence Report. There needs to be better communication between Healthcare staff and disciplinary staff as to the purpose of an Intelligence Report. Some criteria need to be developed and a system in place. An appropriate audit system needs to be in place.","incomplete intelligence report process",""],[7504,2884,"The processes and systems for reducing access to illegal substances need to be improved and tightened up","unrestricted access to illegal substances",""],[7505,2884,"The processes for referrals by both prisoners and staff to psychosocial services needs to be tightened up and improved","missed referrals to psychosocial services",""],[7506,2884,"The standard and accuracy of record keeping by both disciplinary and Healthcare staff needs to be improved","inaccurate record keeping",""]]